<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Turkestan Governorate-General</h1><p class="st-meta">1867 CE – 1917 CE · capital Tashkent</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Russian colonial government of Central Asia, ruled from Tashkent, which turned the region's oases into a cotton economy.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After Russian forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> in 1865, the Turkestan Governorate-General was created in 1867 under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-von-kaufmann">Konstantin von Kaufmann</a>. It expanded through the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> in 1868 and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kokand">Khanate of Kokand</a> in 1876, and in the late 1890s absorbed the Transcaspian region, conquered after the storming of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-geok-tepe">Geok Tepe</a> in 1881.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The governor-general held wide military and civil powers, with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-bukhara">Emirate of Bukhara</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-khiva">Khanate of Khiva</a> left as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorates</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> built the Trans-Caspian and Orenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> railways and promoted American <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>, which became the region's main crop. Muslim courts and customs were mostly left in place, but Russian settlers took land on the steppe. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jadidism">Jadid</a> movement campaigned for educational reform.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>A revolt in 1916 against wartime labour conscription was brutally suppressed. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-revolution">Russian Revolution of 1917</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent-soviet">Tashkent Soviet</a> seized power, and the region became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/turkestan-assr">Turkestan ASSR</a> in 1918.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/turkestan-governorate-general.jpg" alt="Turkestan Governorate-General" width="320" height="210"><figcaption>Image: WuraddoRudotu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Governorate-General_of_Turkestan.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1867 CE – 1917 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tashkent</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Konstantin von Kaufmann, Mikhail Chernyayev, Aleksey Kuropatkin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Russian Orthodoxy</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian, Chagatai Turkic, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, <a href="/countries/kazakhstan">Kazakhstan</a>, <a href="/countries/kyrgyzstan">Kyrgyzstan</a>, <a href="/countries/tajikistan">Tajikistan</a>, <a href="/countries/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Russian Turkestan, Governorate-General of Turkestan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1892&amp;focus=turkestan-governorate-general" aria-label="Turkestan Governorate-General on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6371 704 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Turkestan Governorate-General lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6691 960L6487 457M6691 960L6691 960"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6487 457h0M6691 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6691 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6691 960h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tashkent. <a href="/atlas?year=1892&amp;focus=turkestan-governorate-general">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
